# The data of a launch may be an anonymous Structure written in parentheses (R21, item 4; plan M11 5b): it is that
# Structure as written, given by name to the record of a launch by name and as an operand of the receiver call -- in a
# callable's code and at the root. As the only positional argument of a record it is read by P0 as the record's tail
# (`Add((int: v 7))` is `Add: int: v 7`), whose one field is a place.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places, the call
# main() and the launch of Add by the path main\data\Add.
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
# Structure as written, given by name to the record of a launch by name and as an operand of the receiver call -- in a
# callable's code and at the root.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the anonymous written Structure is the single actual of the record launch `Host\Add((int: v 5))`:
# its field v names the input v of the data parent(Add) = Host (the opened reading of a structural call, step 21.7 K2,
# S2) -- in a callable's code and at the root. The sum takes 5 + 3 = 8, then 8 + 4 = 12: Observed\seen 8,
# Observed\after 12. The former `call((int: v 3); Add)` supplied the literal as data; no form of call supplies data.
# Norm: the book #structural-call (`C(args)`: written actual arguments by the common algorithm), #declaration-selection.
Observed:
    int: seen 0
    int: after 0
end: Observed
Total:
    int: sum 0
end: Total
Host:
    int: v 0
    Add:
        Total\sum := Total\sum + v
    end: Add
end: Host
fn: f () int
    Host\Add((int: v 5))
    Host\Add((int: v 3))
    return: Total\sum
Main:
    Observed\seen := f()
    Host\Add((int: v 4))
    Observed\after := Total\sum
